      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-262819",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose we want to show that the partition function is not additive. To do that, we check if the following equality is true:\n$p(5 + 4) = p(5) + p(4)$\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below. For the left-hand side, we have $p(5 + 4) = 30$.\n\nFor the right-hand side, $p(5) =$ {{field-1}} and $p(4) =$ {{field-2}}.\n\nTherefore, $p(5 + 4)$ {{field-3}} $p(5) + p(4)$."
